{
  "source": "Basch E, Becker C, Rogak LJ, Schrag D, Reeve BB, Spears P, Smith ML, Gounder MM, Mahoney MR, Schwartz GK, Bennett AV, Mendoza TR, Cleeland CS, Sloan JA, Bruner DW, Schwab G, Atkinson TM, Thanarajasingam G, Bhatnagar V, Dueck AC. Composite grading algorithm for the National Cancer Institute's Patient-Reported Outcomes version of the Common Terminology Criteria for Adverse Events (PRO-CTCAE). Clin Trials. 2021;18(1):104-114. doi:10.1177/1740774520975120. PMID 33258687. Lookup rows reproduced row-for-row from the reference implementation of that algorithm shipped in the ProAE R package (Langlais B, Noble B, Truman M, Voss M, Dueck A; CRAN, v1.0.4; internal object comp_tab, 179 rows = the 179 score combinations named in the paper's abstract), retrieved 2026-10-10.",
  "rationale": "PRO-CTCAE items report up to three attributes (frequency, severity, interference) on 0-4 scales. The published composite grading algorithm maps each attribute combination to a single 0-3 grade so that patient-reported symptoms can sit beside clinician CTCAE grades. The tables below are the published lookup reproduced verbatim (reproduced_verbatim = true); nothing was approximated. The published algorithm also carries an explicit zero rule: when the gating attribute (frequency for items that ask frequency, otherwise severity) is 0, the composite is 0 regardless of the other attributes; the lookup tables therefore list the gating attribute only from 1 upward plus the all-zero row. Items with a single attribute use the attribute-specific published mapping; note that the frequency-only mapping (used by our diarrhea item) differs from the severity-only mapping. The 'presence' mapping (yes/no items such as rash and fever/chills) is NOT part of the published algorithm, which does not composite-grade yes/no items; Interim's convention is present -> composite 1 (provisional grade 1, investigator to confirm). Interim maps composite -> provisional CTCAE grade in composite_to_grade.json; that crosswalk is an approximation and is listed in docs/WHAT_IT_GETS_WRONG.md.",
  "reproduced_verbatim": true,
  "retrieved_at": "2026-10-10",
  "scales": {
    "frequency": {
      "0": "Never",
      "1": "Rarely",
      "2": "Occasionally",
      "3": "Frequently",
      "4": "Almost constantly"
    },
    "severity": {
      "0": "None",
      "1": "Mild",
      "2": "Moderate",
      "3": "Severe",
      "4": "Very severe"
    },
    "interference": {
      "0": "Not at all",
      "1": "A little bit",
      "2": "Somewhat",
      "3": "Quite a bit",
      "4": "Very much"
    },
    "presence": {
      "0": "No",
      "1": "Yes"
    }
  },
